notes = "Kickstart ROMs are found by their contents, under any file name, in system/turbouae/kickstarts and in the system directory itself. Without one the built-in AROS ROM is used.|Data files (settings screen, on-screen keyboard, WHDLoad booter) belong in system/turbouae.|Default buttons: L2 = TurboUAE settings, R2 = on-screen keyboard (core options, Input)."

description = "Amiga emulator with a working 68k JIT compiler for 64-bit ARM, made for the R36S and other RK3326 handhelds: Amiberry v3.3 with the TurboUAE fixes (JIT fault handling, protected memory holes), as a libretro core. About 14x the speed of the interpreter on a Cortex-A35 - enough for a 68060-class Workbench with RTG. Core options cover model, CPU/JIT, memory, chipset, video, audio, media and input; the complete Amiberry settings screen and an on-screen Amiga keyboard are built in."
